title: 'Latent: a stale queue key drops the drain without rescheduling'
updated: 2026-08-13T01:50:43Z
---

Found while working on 11. In _drain_queue the line "my $entry = $self->{entries}{$key} or return;" abandons the whole drain when a queued key has no entry, instead of skipping that key and carrying on, so the rest of the queue stalls. Currently unreachable: a key is pruned only when it is not queued, and the queued flag keeps a key at most once in the queue. It is a trap for whoever loosens the prune conditions later. Cheap fix is next rather than return; worth a test that queues a key with no entry and asserts the following key still reconciles.
